corresponding to total assets, total liabilities and total equity.
      The quotient systems of an accounting system A correspond to equivalence
relations or partitions of the set {a1 , a2 ,…, an } of all accounts. There is a well-known
lattice structure on the set of all equivalence relations on a set. Here, a lattice is a
poset with least upper bounds and greatest lower bounds. The partial order on equiva-
lence relations is just set inclusion, while the least upper bound of the equivalence
relations E1 and E2 is the equivalence closure of their union and the greatest lower
bound is their intersection.
      Thus, there is a hierarchy of quotient systems of A corresponding to the lattice
of equivalence relations or partitions. At the lowest level is the identity relation
wherein an account is equivalent only to itself. At the highest level is the universal
